## Why This Is Asked
Auditing and non-repudiation in CNF gateways are critical for multi-tenant environments. This question validates practical expertise with Kubernetes Secrets, HMAC signing, sidecar log pipelines, and retention configuration—essential skills for implementing post-deployment security controls.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped auditing and non-repudiation
- HMAC signing using per-tenant Kubernetes Secrets
- Sidecar-based log forwarding to in-cluster sinks
- ConfigMap-driven log retention and namespace scoping

## Code Example
```javascript
const crypto = require('crypto');
function signLog(logLine, secret) {
  return crypto.createHmac('sha256', secret)
    .update(logLine)
    .digest('hex');
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to design per-tenant runtime feature controls using a Redis-backed flag store with TTL-based caching. It evaluates understanding of multi-tenancy, caching strategies, fallback logic, and operational observability in a CNF gateway context.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant feature flags in a Kubernetes sidecar architecture
- Redis key design using tenantID:path format
- TTL-based caching with 60-second expiration
- Fallback mechanism to global default flags
- Runtime observability via /flags/status endpoint

## Code Example

```javascript
// Feature flag evaluation in CNF sidecar
class FeatureFlagService {
  constructor(redisClient) {
    this.redis = redisClient;
    this.globalDefault = true;
  }

  async evaluateFlag(tenantId, path) {
    const key = `${tenantId}:${path}`;
    const cached = await this.redis.get(key);

    if (cached !== null) {
      return cached === 'true';
    }

    return this.globalDefault;
  }

  async getStatus(tenantId) {
    const flags = await this.redis.keys(`${tenantId}:*`);
    const activeFlags = await Promise.all(
      flags.map(async (key) => ({
        path: key.split(':')[1],
        enabled: (await this.redis.get(key)) === 'true',
        ttl: await this.redis.ttl(key)
      }))
    );

    return {
      tenantId,
      flags: activeFlags,
      timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
    };
  }
}
```

## Redis Seed Configuration

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: redis-seed
  namespace: cnf-system
data:
  seed.sh: |
    #!/bin/bash
    redis-cli SET "tenant-a:/api/v1/features" "true" EX 60
    redis-cli SET "tenant-a:/api/v2/features" "false" EX 60
    redis-cli SET "tenant-b:/api/v1/features" "true" EX 60
```

## Validation Manifest

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: cnf-validation
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: flag-validator
  namespace: cnf-validation
spec:
  containers:
  - name: validator
    image: curlimages/curl:latest
    command: ['sh', '-c']
    args:
      - |
        echo "Testing /flags/status endpoint..."
        curl -s http://cnf-gateway:8080/flags/status | jq .
        echo "\nValidation complete"
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: cnf-gateway
  namespace: cnf-validation
spec:
  ports:
  - port: 8080
    targetPort: 8080
  selector:
    app: cnf-gateway
```
